[2026-08-11 13:03:46] [agentic_pipeline.py (510)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1210041] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nYou are Player 1.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N7\nN3 -> N0, N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N4\nN4 -> N8\nN7 -> N3, N5\nN5 -> terminal\nN0 -> N6\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, Player 1 can move to N2 or N4. Moving to N4 leads to N8 (terminal), so Player 2 has no move and wins immediately. Moving to N2 leads to N7, then to either N3 or N5. If N7 → N3, then N3 → N0 or N9; N0 → N6 (terminal), N9 → terminal. Either path ends the game on Player 2's turn. If N7 → N5, that ends immediately. So all paths from N2 eventually end on Player 2's turn. Thus, any move from N1 leads to Player 2 winning. However, the goal is to maximize final outcome — meaning avoid losing. Since all moves from N1 lead to Player 2 winning, the best choice is the one that delays the loss longest or minimizes Player 2's advantage. But since all paths end with Player 2 having no move, all moves result in Player 2 winning. Therefore, Player 1 must choose a move that leads to a terminal node as soon as possible to end the game immediately. N4 → N8 (terminal) ends the game on Player 2's turn, so Player 1 wins. Thus, choosing N4 results in Player 1 winning immediately. Therefore, N4 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6876910016977928, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, Player 1 can move to N2 or N4. Moving to N4 leads to N8 (terminal