al destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nYou are Player 2.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N9, N5\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1\nN7 -> N2, N4\nN9 -> N3\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8\nN8 -> N7, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Current node is N5. Player 2 moves second. From N5, legal moves are to N8 or N9. If Player 1 moves to N9, then N9 → N3 → terminal, so Player 2 loses immediately. Thus, Player 2 must avoid that. From N5, moving to N8 is better: N8 → N7 or N6. N6 → terminal (Player 1 loses). If Player 1 responds to N7 → N2 or N4, both lead to terminal (N2 → terminal, N4 → N1 → terminal). So no matter what Player 1 does from N7, Player 2 can eventually force a win. Thus, choosing N8 ensures a win. Moving to N9 is losing. Therefore, optimal move is to N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4056876061120543, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Current node is N5. Player 2 moves second. From N5, legal moves are to N8 or N9. If Player 1 moves to N9, then N9 → N3 → terminal, so Player 2 loses immediately. Thus, Player 2 must avoid that. From N5, moving to N8 is better: N8 → N7 or N6. N6 → terminal (Player 1 loses). If Player 1 responds to N7 → N2 or N4, both lead to terminal (N2 → terminal, N4 → N1 → terminal). So no matter what Player 1 does from N7, Player 2 can eventually force a win. Thus, choosing N8 ensures a win. Moving to N9 is losing. Therefore, optimal move is to N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nYou are Player 1.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N9, N5\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1\nN7 -> N2, N4\nN9 -> N3\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8\nN8 -> N7, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, Player 1 can move to N7 or N6. Moving to N6 leads to terminal (Player 2 has no move and loses), so this is a winning move. Moving to N7 leads to N2 or N4. N2 is terminal, so if Player 1 goes to N7 and then Player 2 goes to N2, Player 1 wins. But if Player 2 goes to N4, then N1 (terminal), Player 1 wins again. However, the immediate win is by going directly to N6, which ends the game immediately. Thus, N6 is the best choice.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4370967741935483, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, Player 1 can move to N7 or N6. Moving to N6 leads to terminal (Player 2 has no move and loses), so this is a winning move. Moving to N7 leads to N2 or N4. N2 is terminal, so if Player 1 goes to N7 and then Player 2 goes to N2, Player 1 wins. But if Player 2 goes to N4, then N1 (terminal), Player 1 wins again. However, the immediate win is by going directly to N6, which ends the game immediately. Thus, N6 is the best choice.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nYou are Player 1.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N